gt.blockmachines.matterblueprints.multimachine.host.name=Multiblock Machine Host
gt.blockmachines.matterblueprints.multimachine.host.tooltip=Machine Type: §eRemote Multiblock Host§r\nRuns explicitly bound machines of one type from centralized I/O and power hatches\nConsumers use central energy hatches or an owner-powered wireless upgrade\nSeparate machine and upgrade slots; the upgrade makes central energy hatches optional\nGenerators use central dynamos, not the wireless network\nSupports turbine, naquadah, gas and liquid-fuel multiblock generators while retaining rotor, fuel, coolant, warm-up, efficiency and pollution mechanics\nSupports Space Assembler MK-I/MK-II/MK-III modules while they remain connected to the Space Elevator\nOrdinary remotes keep their power hatches for rating; Space Assemblers use their fixed module voltage\nBatch mode is supported; disabling work finishes current jobs; progress is shown in seconds\nChemical Plants use central Catalyst Housings without catalyst consumption, wear or empty carriers\nRemote plants need no catalysts; hosted plants must have identical tiers and voltage\n§7§m-----------------------------------------\n§eBinding setup:\n§f1. Craft and hold a Hosted Machine Binder\n§f2. Shift-left-click the host controller to record it\n§f3. Right-click a remote controller to add or remove it\n§f4. Drone DownLinks only provide maintenance and never auto-host machines\n§7§m-----------------------------------------\nHold §l[LSHIFT]§r§7 to display structure guidance
gt.blockmachines.matterblueprints.multimachine.host.tooltip_secondary=§fSize: §617§7x§65§7x§65§7 (§6L§7x§6W§7x§6H§7), hollow interior\n§fStructure:\n   §fController: §7Front middle-right, facing outward\n   §6137 §fFlowing Data-Light Casings: §7Edges and complete bottom layer\n   §627 §fHosted Cooling Fans: §7Wall fan band\n   §632+ §fHosted Machine-Room Casings: §7Replaceable hatch positions\n   §eExactly 1 §fMaintenance Hatch: §7Any replaceable position\n   §eConsumer hosting (optional with wireless upgrade): §fnormal, multi-amp or laser Energy Hatch: §7Any replaceable position\n   §eGenerator hosting: §fnormal Dynamo or Laser Source Hatch: §7Any replaceable position\n   §e1+ §fInput Bus or Input Hatch: §7Any replaceable position\n   §e1+ §fOutput Bus or Output Hatch: §7Any replaceable position\n§7§m------------------------------\n§fUse the Multiblock Structure §9Hologram §1Projector§f on the controller to visualize/build it!
